+## 9. Replay-probe results — off vs A (greedy), :8089, 4 phases, fresh server each
+
+Server cmd: production yaml cmd with `${PORT}->8089`, `LLAMA_ATTN_ROT_DISABLE=1`, plus
+`--spec-type ngram-mod` (A). mmproj loaded (`--mmproj --no-mmproj-offload`); **spec ran
+fine on text-only traffic, no mmproj refusal** (draft_n>0 and 24 "accepted N/M draft
+tokens (restore checkpoint)" lines in `server_single-agent.log`). `draft_n`/
+`draft_n_accepted` present only when n_draft_tokens>0 (server-common.cpp:82-85), else
+0.
+
+Foreground decode tok/s (sum predicted_n / sum predicted_ms), A vs off:
+
+| phase | off fg | A fg | A bg | A fg draft acceptance |
+|-------|-------:|-----:|-----:|:----------------------|
+| single-agent | 55.1 | **86.0** | — | 75% (8229/6212) |
+| single-mem | 55.6 | 53.1 | — | 9% (740/69) |
+| dual-agent | 26.3 | 25.5 | 26.8 | 14% (1856/259) |
+| dual-mem | 25.0 | 23.8 | 26.1 | 9% (740/69) |
+
+- **single-agent +56%** (55.1 -> 86.0): long agent contexts with repeated file/diff/
+  test text draft well.
+- **dual phases: no gain, slight loss** (26.3 -> 25.5; 25.0 -> 23.8). This is the
+  decision metric (both slots busy). Low fg acceptance (14% agent, 9% mem) means most
+  drafted tokens are rejected, so draft work is mostly overhead while the GPU is
+  batch-shared across the two slots.
+- `length` finishes (spec may emit more tokens than the off arm): off single-agent 1
